     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum daily dose. At that level the risk of serious harm is high, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. More ibuprofen also doesn't give more pain relief. The analgesic effect plateaus at lower doses.\n\nIf you have a clinical reason I'm not seeing, the next step is to discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. They can approve an off-label dose through the right channel.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the max)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the goal is stronger analgesia, I can also enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at a standard dose. Tell me which you'd like."
      }
